0 @NOTE1@ NOTE
1 CONT Fixture for #687: one real place appears under several PLAC forms so the
1 CONT import should consolidate them into a single place note rather than one
1 CONT note per spelling. Expected place notes after import (8 total):
1 CONT   - Canada
1 CONT   - Quebec (province)  <- "Québec, Canada" + "Quebec, Canada"
1 CONT   - Ontario            <- abbreviations Ont. / ON all expand to Ontario
1 CONT   - Nova Scotia        <- abbreviation NS expands to Nova Scotia
1 CONT   - Montreal (city)    <- Montréal/Montreal + QC/PQ; variants in historical_names
1 CONT   - Quebec (city)      <- "Québec, Québec, Canada" + "Quebec, Quebec, Canada"
1 CONT   - Toronto            <- Ontario / Ont. / ON forms all collapse
1 CONT   - Halifax            <- Nova Scotia / NS forms collapse
1 CONT Quebec the CITY and Quebec the PROVINCE must stay SEPARATE (a leaf-only
1 CONT match is never merged). The Montreal and Quebec-city notes should each
1 CONT carry their discarded spellings under historical_names.
